{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T11:21:54.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1781"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1781: secret guard reports a single-quoted reference in compact JSON, and a value of seven backslashes, as password_assignment on 2026.11.25"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Follow-up to GH-1775 (fixed in 2026.11.25). Two neighbouring shapes that returned no finding on 2026.11.14 are reported as password_assignment on 2026.11.25. First, a single-quoted run-time reference inside a JSON string in compact form: title 'password': '${BUILD_PASSWORD}' followed directly by the next member; pretty JSON, a title-only object and the double-quoted twin stay clean, so the verdict depends on serialization. Second, a single-quoted value made only of backslashes: seven backslashes (an unterminated value, since the last quote is escaped) is reported where 2026.11.14 reported nothing; six stay clean and eight were already reported. Reading: the single-quoted value is not ended at its own closing quote when it sits inside a JSON string, and an escape-only value is judged as a literal secret."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["false-positive","gh:1781","sdk","secret-guard"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-26T11:21:54.325Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T11:21:54.325Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The four JSON forms of the single-quoted reference return no findings; Single-quoted values of six and seven backslashes return no findings; a literal password is still reported; A differential against the published 2026.11.14 bundle shows no other verdict change for the reported shapes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-doxj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":80},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A pure run-time reference in a single-quoted value is clean in every JSON serialization, and an escape-only value carries no secret finding, as on 2026.11.14"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Compact JSON with a single-quoted reference and a seven-backslash single-quoted value report password_assignment"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1775","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-26T11:21:54.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4ba7545ca5e3538aee1f40e2d7e7b6d2a572b58a7d01e26bc0fd1ca460ec5413","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5286b3a86e237d92a7581f66550d535f98e5f7793ad004140c5ed9e4ade0b015"}
