{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T15:59:07.425Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T15:59:07.424Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 on PR #1789 (gpt-6.2-sol xhigh), both P1 findings confirmed and fixed. (1) example foo\"[\" --'password'=${EMPTY}\",\"\"<literal>\": the lexer declines the quote after foo (a quote after a word character opens no string), so the quote after [ opened a phantom container string whose close cut the literal; main still reported it through the uncut structured reading, while its flat twin (--password=...) was already missed since GH-1775. Fix: the lexer records a declined quote per kind until the line ends, and enclosingStringClose trusts no string of that kind opened later on the line (trustsOpenString); both spellings are reported again. (2) the Python dict fixture in secret-guard-string-boundaries.spec.ts (a password of two unrecognized escapes, an escaped apostrophe and four characters): Python keeps unrecognized escapes (nine characters), the decoded reading drops them (seven) and the first-quote raw reading stopped at the escaped quote; main reported it through the escape-aware raw span. Fix: that backslash-kept span is read again whenever the escape-aware scan closes the literal, alongside the first-quote reading; it is skipped only for a span left open by an escaped last quote, which is what produced the seven-backslash false positive. P3 docs: the first-quote reading is described as TOML's and a scanner approximation for YAML. Differential rerun: 276 changes versus 2026.11.25, all finding to none, none literal-bearing, no new findings; the four that reverted to the 2026.11.25 verdict are a seven-backslash value inside a malformed single-quoted repr, where the escape-aware scan closes the span."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T15:59:07.425Z"}],"before_hash":"b8652547d66da41a3215a5d5e9b9859d1928871bf763630160d0e83a2096b497","after_hash":"1c6517b421845eb4868859505f495f4e64e3b426f5484439fe7e7ed2e424af35","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a3ffb467162f9fab42240853dac0be4db28b1fddcb1c16e2ae2ebbd5a0a28768","reanchor_evidence":[{"before_hash":"b8652547d66da41a3215a5d5e9b9859d1928871bf763630160d0e83a2096b497","after_hash":"5df9d9037a76d4dd6d036d2611bf146c19002c602b054b11b76195a91ff3d387","patch_hash":"e8b19d95814c0e273b0d6ef6971c86e8edc2db1f9e9da1a59f8fba7d1ded75c5","hash_algorithm":"sha256","item_hash_version":3},{"before_hash":"b8652547d66da41a3215a5d5e9b9859d1928871bf763630160d0e83a2096b497","after_hash":"7efef47d1297f188091b9cf8e2cb80483293e78c18b1c53220a497d7f2ba2a86","patch_hash":"e4c4178509bf68ebccdade26b64fffb14bea0bf8cb8e559f7900ed1cc084ffa9","hash_algorithm":"sha256","item_hash_version":3}]}
