{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.174Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 on PR #1789: both secret-guard findings confirmed against main and fixed. (1) A shell option whose single-quoted piece ends in an escaped-looking backslash and has characters joined after it (the round-2 printf fixture in secret-guard-string-boundaries.spec.ts) was reported on main and missed here: the first-quote reading could not see the joined characters, and the backslash-kept span is skipped when left open. The value judge now also applies the text reading to single-quoted literals with backslashes; it is the shell-word and TOML reading (first closing quote, joined pieces kept), and it replaces the separate first-quote reading. (2) A Python raw-string prefix before a JSON-like line (r-quoted text, then a dict member holding a bare reference) was newly reported: one declined quote distrusted every later string on the line. Now only the next string of that kind after an odd run of declined quotes is suspect, and a Python string prefix (r, b, u, f and their two-letter pairs, any case) opens its string, with backslash escapes as Python reads them. lexStep's quote opening moved into openOrDecline to stay within the complexity budget. Differential: 428 changes versus 2026.11.25, none on a literal-bearing value; 152 new findings, all either a quoted literal password inside JSON text that both published versions missed, or backslash-only values in malformed single-quoted reprs where 2026.11.25 already reports the backslash-free spellings."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.175Z"}],"before_hash":"1c6517b421845eb4868859505f495f4e64e3b426f5484439fe7e7ed2e424af35","after_hash":"eb6a6eba3db41c5f35fefa7f810dc28db0ab6d65046ba116c61433234fa8d732","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"db6c5824085dbcdf21adaf98cc05baad16f04811a9f5a8acb7759f42dfa68c73"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.168Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.167Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 on PR #1789: two synthetic shell lines desynchronized the narrowed round-2 rule (a second quoted shell argument after a declined quote re-opened a trusted phantom string; a Python-prefixed single quote forced Python escapes where the shell closes the string), and both lost findings main reported. The lexer now follows one principle instead of per-case narrowing: a cut only removes findings, so it is made only where the string state is unambiguous; a line that declined a quote of a kind reads as shell, and no later string of that kind on the line is trusted. Python prefixes still open their string, with the escapes an unprefixed one has. Both lines are in secret-guard-string-boundaries.spec.ts; the round-2 Python-prefix case stays clean; the 18,816-input differential is unchanged from round 2."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.168Z"}],"before_hash":"eb6a6eba3db41c5f35fefa7f810dc2